1 NOTE [FT_Art_Na_MAacioch.FTW]   Granny was a fairly formidable lady, with strong black hair, who liked to play cards at times with her grandchildren by the light of a tilley lamp in the kitchen at Ballure.
2 CONC  She died in hospital in Lifford in 1966, having been ill for a brief period. The Ballure house was originally in Granny's family, and Grandad moved there following their marriage. The house was origi
2 CONC nally a single storey cottage but was rebuilt by Grandad as a two storey house in 1932. Uncle John undertook  a major revamp of the house in the early 1980s after Grandad's death.
