1 NOTE <p>DF</p><p><p>Notes for PATRICK (PAT DONIE) FRIEL:</p></p><p><p>Pat is recorded in both the 1901 and 1911 Census. He moved to live in McConigley's in Ballure when he married Maryanne, one of the thre
2 CONC e McConigley sisters - Bridget and Sally being the others. He rebuilt the McConigley house in 1932, and continued to live there until his death in 1980. He was a small stocky man with a limp, relative
2 CONC ly quiet, and always giving the impression of being at ease with himself and the world. Dad frequently mentioned that he had worked as a "sapper" - possibly working for the Ordnance Survey and working
2 CONC  as far away as Tyrone. In latter years, he would sit for long periods at the turf fire in the house in Ballure, smoking his pipe and spitting occasionally into the flames. He survived the amputation 
2 CONC of one of his legs in his early 90's, and was confined to a wheelchair thereafter.</p><p></p>
