1 NOTE <p>DF</p><p><p>Notes for MARY (PAT) FRIEL:</p></p><p><p>Mary was the eldest of the family. Dad remembers her as being frequently unwell - query if she contacted TB. (Note Sept 2007 - Peggy stated that
2 CONC  Mary had had polio and that she had a small limp as a consequence.) She was looked after by nuns, possibly in Derry, for a period but they did not keep her - she may have gone to join them but may ha
2 CONC ve been rejected on health grounds. Dad says that she as quiet and had lovely long brown hair, though she also had lumps on her wrist and on the back of her knee which he wondered might be realted to 
2 CONC her illness - which he also suggested might have been cancer-related. She was unmarried. There is some confusion re her age, though it is given on her grave in Massmount as 23 when she died. Her date 
2 CONC of birth is noted as April 1913 in the Ballymichael School records.</p><p></p>
