1 NOTE <p>DF</p><p><p>Notes for WILLIAM (WILLIE DONIE) FRIEL:</p></p><p><p>Grand Uncle Willie was a lightkeeper, who lived in Fahan in his retirement in a bungalow overlooking Lough Swilly. He is in the 1901
2 CONC  Census as a farmers son, unmarried, who could read and write both Irish and English. He was not on the 1911 Census. Eileen Carragher believes that Willie eloped with Kitty as the local priest refused
2 CONC  to marry them. This was on the grounds that they were cousins. There is William Friel in the 1911 census aged 27, living in Donaghadee, a single lightkeeper.</p><p></p>
