2 CONC ith some of his brothers - possibly Eddie, but there is no record of this.  When asked in September 2007 as to what became of him, Peggy, his niece stated simply that "he died" - suggesting that he di
2 CONC ed young in Ballure - possible sometime pre 1900.</p><p></p>
